  "text": "But automating the check is only half the story. We packaged it as what we call an agentic skill basically a tool an AI coding assistant can pick up and use on its own. And that changes what it's good for. Anyone with a coding agent and this skill could build, in an afternoon, a plugin inside Rhino or Revit that gives you live feedback as you draw; or a little stand-alone app where you drop in a plan and get a score; or just bolt a furnishability check onto some product that already exists. And it's all open-source, under Apache 2.0. We genuinely see this as one of the project's big outcomes in its own right completely separate from training our own model.",
